 # Changelog
 
+## 1.6.0
+
+- Ticket assignment. `PUT /tickets/:id/assignee` with `{"assignee": "<agent>"}` assigns an open or in-progress ticket to an
+  agent (a name of at most 64 characters), and `{"assignee": null}` unassigns it; other tickets answer 409. Assigning the
+  agent a ticket already has changes nothing. The agent is notified (`ticket.assigned`), and the change is in the audit log.
+- Tickets show `assignee` (null when unassigned) with `ASSIGNEES=on`; without it a ticket shows it once it has had an
+  assignee, so tickets nobody assigns look as in 1.5.0.
+- `GET /tickets?assignee=<agent>` lists an agent's tickets, `?assignee=` the unassigned ones. A ticket must now match every
+  filter given: before, the listing kept a ticket that matched any one of them, against the API documentation.
+- The command line shows the assignee in `list` (a column; in `list --raw` a fifth column after the title) and `show`, and
+  takes `--assignee`.
+- The data file keeps `assignee` on tickets that have had one; the format stays version 1 and 1.5.0 ignores the field.
+
 ## 1.5.0
 
 - Due times ([decision 9](docs/decisions/0009-due-times.md)). Every ticket gets a due time, `due`: the time it was created
