+### Assign a ticket: `PUT /tickets/:id/assignee`
+
+```json
+{ "assignee": "sam" }
+```
+
+`assignee` is an agent's name (not empty, at most 64 characters, one line) or null, which unassigns the ticket. Answers 200
+with the ticket. Only an `open` or `in_progress` ticket can be assigned or unassigned; any other is 409 `conflict`. A bad
+body is 400 `invalid`. Assigning the agent the ticket already has (or unassigning an unassigned ticket) changes nothing: no
+audit entry, no notification, and `updated` stays. Otherwise the change is audited (`ticket.assigned`, with the field
+`assignee`), and the agent the ticket was assigned to is notified; unassigning notifies nobody.
